ONE WORD SUBSTITUTION (1–20)
1. A person who cannot read or write
✅ Word: Illiterate
Hinglish Meaning: Jo padh-likh nahi sakta.
Learning Trick: Letter nahi padh sakta → Illiterate
Example: Many villagers were illiterate.
PYQ: ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐ (Bahut important)
2. A person who knows many languages
✅ Polyglot
Meaning: Jo bahut saari languages bol sakta hai.
Trick: Poly = Many (Polygon = many sides)
Example: She is a polyglot and speaks six languages.
PYQ: ⭐⭐⭐⭐
3. A person who writes with both hands
✅ Ambidextrous
Meaning: Dono haathon se equally likh sakta hai.
Trick: Think Ambi = Both (Ambidextrous = both hands)
Example: He is ambidextrous.
PYQ: ⭐⭐⭐⭐
4. One who loves mankind
✅ Philanthropist
Meaning: Jo logon ki bhalai karta hai.
Trick: Phil = Love, Anthro = Human
Example: Ratan Tata was known as a philanthropist.
PYQ: ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐
5. One who hates mankind
✅ Misanthrope
Meaning: Jo logon se nafrat karta hai.
Trick: Mis = Hate, Anthrope = Humans
Example: He became a misanthrope after many betrayals.
PYQ: ⭐⭐⭐
6. One who believes in God
✅ Theist
Meaning: Bhagwan par vishwas rakhne wala.
Trick: Theo = God
Example: He is a theist.
PYQ: ⭐⭐⭐⭐
7. One who does not believe in God
✅ Atheist
Meaning: Bhagwan ko nahi maanta.
Trick: A = Not + Theist
Example: He declared himself an atheist.
PYQ: ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐
8. One who studies stars and planets
✅ Astronomer
Meaning: Taare aur planets ka study karta hai.
Trick: Astro = Stars
Example: Aryabhata was a famous astronomer.
PYQ: ⭐⭐⭐⭐
9. One who travels from place to place
✅ Itinerant
Meaning: Jo ek jagah tikta nahi, ghoomta rehta hai.
Trick: Imagine an itinerary = travel plan.
Example: He lived an itinerant life.
PYQ: ⭐⭐⭐
10. One who cannot pay debts
✅ Insolvent
Meaning: Karz chukane ke paise na hona.
Trick: In + Solvent = paisa solve nahi kar pa raha.
Example: The company became insolvent.
PYQ: ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐
11. A person who eats everything
✅ Omnivore
Meaning: Veg + Non-Veg dono khata hai.
Trick: Omni = All
Example: Bears are omnivores.
PYQ: ⭐⭐⭐⭐
12. A person who eats only plants
✅ Herbivore
Meaning: Sirf paudhe khata hai.
Trick: Herb = Plants
Example: A cow is a herbivore.
PYQ: ⭐⭐⭐
13. A person who eats only meat
✅ Carnivore
Meaning: Sirf maans khata hai.
Trick: Carni = Meat
Example: A lion is a carnivore.
PYQ: ⭐⭐⭐
14. A person who lives alone
✅ Recluse
Meaning: Akela rehna pasand karta hai.
Trick: Re-close → Khud ko sabse close kar leta hai.
Example: He lived like a recluse.
PYQ: ⭐⭐⭐⭐
15. One who cannot hear
✅ Deaf
Meaning: Behra.
Trick: Simple daily-use word.
Example: He is deaf by birth.
PYQ: ⭐⭐⭐⭐
16. One who cannot speak
✅ Dumb / Mute (Exam me "Mute" zyada appropriate hota hai.)
Meaning: Bol nahi sakta.
Trick: Mute = Sound muted.
Example: The child was mute.
PYQ: ⭐⭐⭐
17. One who cannot see
✅ Blind
Meaning: Andha.
Trick: Common word.
Example: The blind man crossed the road.
PYQ: ⭐⭐⭐⭐
18. One who looks on the bright side
✅ Optimist
Meaning: Hamesha positive sochne wala.
Trick: Optimum = Best
Example: Stay an optimist.
PYQ: ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐
19. One who looks on the dark side
✅ Pessimist
Meaning: Hamesha negative sochne wala.
Trick: Pessimistic = Negative
Example: Don't be a pessimist.
PYQ: ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐
20. One who talks too much
✅ Garrulous
Meaning: Bahut zyada bolne wala.
Trick: Imagine someone saying "Grr...rr..." bina ruke bol raha hai.
Example: The old man was garrulous.
